warning[NK1350]: `p` is a `P`, which copies by itself: `.clone()` makes nothing new.
   --> tests/fix_needless_clone.nika:20:13
    |
 20 |     let q = p.clone()
    |             ^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A number, a `bool`, a `char` and a type whose every part copies are copied wherever they are read (ADR-294 D9.1).
    = help: Delete `.clone()`.
warning[NK1350]: This `.clone()` is the last use of `s`: it copies `s` only to drop it.
   --> tests/fix_needless_clone.nika:23:18
    |
 23 |     println(take(s.clone()))
    |                  ^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: Nothing reads `s` after it, so it can be handed over itself.
    = help: Hand `s` itself: write `s` for `s.clone()`.
warning[NK1350]: `xs` is copied only to be walked: nothing in the loop changes it or takes it.
   --> tests/fix_needless_clone.nika:25:14
    |
 25 |     for x in xs.clone() {
    |              ^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A `for` over a place lends its elements (ADR-094 D4), so the loop can walk the place itself.
    = help: Delete `.clone()`.
